cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BFO-Aligned ValueNet
message: >-
  If you use the BFO-aligned ValueNet ontology suite, please cite it using
  these metadata. This record covers the project-authored suite only. The
  original DUL-aligned ValueNet is separate upstream work with its own
  authorship; cite it directly rather than through this entry.
type: software
abstract: >-
  An ontology of human values aligned to the Basic Formal Ontology. Values
  are modelled as realizable entities that inhere in an agent and are
  realized in processes of appraisal, choice, feeling, and action, rather
  than as labels attached to things. The suite reuses Common Core
  Ontologies terms for the information entities that carry textual
  evidence, and records annotation-level correspondences to the original
  ValueNet vocabulary.
repository-code: https://github.com/Skreen5hot/ValueNet
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

# Authorship is the repository owner's to state, not this file's to infer.
# The entry below is the account the commits are made under. Before public
# release the owner should confirm the author list, add any co-authors, and
# supply ORCID and affiliation if they want them cited.
authors:
  - alias: Skreen5hot
    given-names: Aaron
    family-names: Damiano

# No release has been tagged for the ontology suite. The repository's
# existing tags mark measurement checkpoints, not ontology releases, and
# citing one would imply a release that has not been made.
#
# Version policy: a citable version is a signed-off Git tag or GitHub
# Release. Until one exists, cite the repository and the commit you used.
# A GitHub Pages build is labelled "latest from main" and is not a release.
#
# When the first ontology release is tagged, add here:
#   version: <tag>
#   date-released: <YYYY-MM-DD>
#   doi: <if minted>

keywords:
  - ontology
  - Basic Formal Ontology
  - BFO
  - human values
  - Schwartz values
  - moral foundations
  - knowledge representation

references:
  - type: software
    title: ValueNet
    notes: >-
      The original DUL-aligned ValueNet, the source tradition this suite
      re-expresses and maps to. Its licence has not been identified; this
      repository grants no rights over it.
    repository-code: https://github.com/StenDoipanni/ValueNet
    authors:
      - given-names: Stefano
        family-names: De Giorgis
  # Computational contributors. Deliberately referenced rather than
  # listed as authors: authorship carries responsibility for the
  # accuracy and integrity of the work, which an AI system cannot
  # assume. Credited in full in ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md.
  - type: software
    title: Claude
    version: Claude Opus 5
    notes: >-
      Substantial assistance with ontology engineering, implementation,
      testing, evidence design, review and documentation. The model
      identifier is the one recorded in the Co-Authored-By trailer of
      the commits it contributed to, not a version reconstructed after
      the fact.
    url: https://www.anthropic.com/claude
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic

  - type: software
    title: Codex
    notes: >-
      Assistance with implementation and code during the repository's
      development. Product-level name only: no model identifier was
      recorded at the time, and none is reconstructed here.
    url: https://openai.com/codex
    authors:
      - name: OpenAI

  - type: software
    title: Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) 2020
    repository-code: https://github.com/BFO-ontology/BFO-2020
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    authors:
      - name: The BFO development team
  - type: software
    title: Common Core Ontologies
    repository-code: https://github.com/CommonCoreOntology/CommonCoreOntologies
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    authors:
      - name: The Common Core Ontologies development team
